lynxpm (0.5.1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  [SECURITY]
  * security(H1): ed25519 release signing — 'lynx update --apply' now
    verifies a .sig companion asset before replacing the binary. Refuses
    unsigned releases unless --insecure-skip-signature is passed.
  * security(H2): unconditional PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS in sandbox wrapper,
    closes setuid escape on kernels without landlock (< 5.13).
  * security(H3): reject absolute logs.stdout/stderr paths; add O_NOFOLLOW
    on log file open to prevent symlink-mediated arbitrary file writes.
  * security(H4): env_file ownership check — absolute env files must be
    owned by the calling UID (blocks cross-tenant secret exfiltration).
  * security(H5): abort sandbox if MS_PRIVATE mount fails — prevents host
    /proc unmount via shared mount propagation.
  * security(H6): per-sandbox private tmpfs over /tmp — isolates same-user
    sandboxes from planting binaries for each other.
  * security(M1): exact asset-name match in updater (was strings.Contains).
  * security(M2): broader package-system detection (dpkg+rpm+pacman, pre-
    and post-symlink paths).
  * security(M3): reject non-absolute cwd in sandbox config.
  * security(M4): refuse XDG_RUNTIME_DIR fallback to /tmp for socket path.
    XDG_RUNTIME_DIR now required; LYNX_SOCKET remains as override.

  [BREAKING CHANGES]
  * 'lynx update --apply' requires --insecure-skip-signature until the
    release workflow publishes signed assets.
  * User-mode daemon now requires XDG_RUNTIME_DIR to be set (standard on
    systemd-logind sessions). Non-login shells (cron, bare ssh) must
    export LYNX_SOCKET to an absolute path in a private directory.

  [FEATURES]
  * feat(cli): --isolation sandbox using user namespaces + landlock + rlimit
    (unprivileged container isolation, no sudo required).
  * feat(cli): global --quiet / -q flag.
  * feat(start): --dry-run / -n previews the resolved spec without contacting
    the daemon.
  * feat(cli): lynx completion <bash|zsh|fish> emits shell completion scripts.
  * feat(install-tools): default to ~/.local/bin, add --system flag for the
    /usr/local/bin path (no longer requires root in the common case).
  * feat(cli): add 'reset' command to zero Restarts counter without restart.
  * feat(cli): add 'scale' command to grow/shrink an app post-hoc.
  * feat(list): add --json flag for machine-readable output.
  * feat(ipc): per-UID token-bucket rate limit on every IPC request (ON by
    default, 200 burst / 100 req/s per UID).
  * feat(daemon): audit log (JSON-lines) for every destructive action.
    ON in system mode to /var/log/lynx-pm/audit.log.
  * feat(start): configurable stop signal (--stop-signal) and graceful
    timeout (--stop-timeout, default 10s).
  * feat(start): resource limits via --memory-max, --cpu-max, --tasks-max.
    Enforced via cgroup v2 (dynamic) or rlimit (sandbox).
  * feat(daemon): size-based log rotation (50 MiB default, 3 backups).
  * ci: GitHub Actions release workflow with ed25519 binary signing.

  [FIXES]
  * fix(daemon): detect system mode by uid 0 OR lynx user. --isolation
    dynamic now works on the shipped .deb (previously rejected because
    lynxd runs as the lynx user, uid != 0).
  * fix(handlers): validate cwd is accessible to the daemon user; replaces
    the cryptic "fork/exec: permission denied" with a clear error.
  * fix(polkit): grant manage-units when the "unit" detail is absent, which
    is the typical case for systemd-run's StartTransientUnit. Unblocks
    --isolation dynamic on the shipped .deb.
  * fix(process): count every restart regardless of trigger (cron ticks
    were not incrementing Restarts).
  * fix(manager): reject duplicate (namespace, name) on start with ERR_CONFLICT.
  * fix(cli): open IPC client lazily — bad invocations no longer emit a
    daemon connection error before the usage message.
  * fix(ipc): replace cryptic dial error with actionable daemon-off hint.
  * docs: add SECURITY.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, runnable examples in --help.

 -- Jaro-c <jaro-c@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 16 Apr 2026 18:00:00 -0500

